{
  "_additions_2026_07": "bitwise-xor::warity was added when ESH-0362 (#357) made a wrong-arity call a FATAL COMPILE error on native. Native now refuses to emit code for the translation unit; the hosted VM still accepts the call and yields a value, so the two engines legitimately disagree on this probe. Recorded explicitly rather than absorbed silently, per the shrink-only ratchet. Closing this gap means making the VM reject wrong arity too \u2014 tracked separately, it is not a native-side defect.",
  "_comment": "P8 axis-3 native-vs-VM known parity gaps; gate fails on any key NOT listed here. Generated by p8_arity_sweep.py --update-baseline --full, then extended by union (never shrunk silently). The 2026-08 extension records the surface exposed by #445 (SW-38/SW-39), which promoted the accessor/string/vector/bitwise builtin families to first-class VM values: those names now answer on the VM, so pre-existing native-side arity/type-contract gaps became observable. Every added key is a wrong-arity or wrong-type call. Tracked follow-up: the hash-keys / hash-values / hash-table-keys / hash-table-values ::wtype entries are native SIGSEGVs on a non-table argument and need a real native fix, not a permanent grandfather.",
